Title: 0011-aros-directory-notification
Repository: pragtical
Base-Commit: 5c05f09e081833b581fb5ecd10e64963dec87f03
Requires: 0010-tokenizer-resume-zero-state.patch
Author: aros-pragtical project
Date: 2026-11-15
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: AROS only: new src/api/dirmonitor/aros.c, backend registration in dirmonitor.c/dirmonitor.h, Meson option choice and source selection. No change for other systems.

Problem:
  On AROS the editor used the dummy directory monitor, so every watched directory and open file was checked by comparing modification times and changes made outside the editor showed up late or not at all.
Solution:
  Add an 'aros' directory monitor backend on dos.library StartNotify/EndNotify. One NotifyRequest per watched path posts to a polled message port; all dos.library calls stay on the main thread. Only the RAM disk and SFS are used, because FAT accepts a directory request but does not report changes to entries inside it; other file systems keep the modification-time fallback.
Validation:
  2026-11-15, built for x86_64 ABIv1, x86_64 ABIv11 and Raspberry Pi. On mainline nightly 20261113 and AROS One 1.3 an event log showed notifications for create, modify and delete in a RAM disk and an SFS directory and for a modified file; a FAT directory is refused and falls back. Project tree updates, the reload prompt and quit with active watches passed on all three targets.
Removal:
  Permanent. The RAM/SFS restriction can go when FAT reports changes inside a watched directory.

